"""Multilingual crop catalogue — categories, languages and crop entries.

Honesty contract (must be preserved by API + UI):
- ``names`` contains best-effort local-language names recalled from general
  knowledge. They are NOT verified against an authoritative source, so the API
  reports every non-English name with status ``"unverified"`` and every absent
  language with status ``"missing"``. Only ``en`` is ``"verified"``.
- ``image`` is resolved at serve time from the bundled manifest
  (frontend/public/images/crops/manifest.json): only entries verified through
  the Commons fetch pipeline (real file page, real author, free license) are
  served as ``verified``; everything else stays ``pending`` with an emoji
  placeholder — never a fabricated photo.
- ``g_en``/``g_te`` are short, hedged, general educational notes — not
  verified against a cited publication. ``guide_verified`` is False for every
  entry; the UI must label them "general guidance" and point farmers to
  ICAR / state agricultural extension services. No citations are invented.
- ``model`` marks the 22 crops that the trained Random Forest can actually
  predict (labels from models/training_stats.json). Catalogue browsing and
  cultivation guides are kept strictly separate from ML predictions.
"""

